I name them like red soft 4 main or red soft 4 br depending on
if I first encountered that type on level 4 of the main branch or
level 4 of a branch.  There's a table of what minimum depth in
the main dungeon each type can appear so finding gems first
in the main dungeon gives extra information.  By checking the
table against what I already know I can end up with definite
identification of a fair number of gems without spending a
scroll or wand or using a touchstone on them.  Specific
combinations of color and hardness give immediate knowledge
of type immediately or once that color's glass is known.

In the end, the exact value of a gem isn't all that important -
Unicorn ID them as glass or valuable, use the glass ones as
missiles, trade the valuable ones at shops, worry about
exact ID at liesure in case you want a handfull of very
valuable ones to ascend with.  The most important aspect
might be controlling luck with unicorns using called or
IDed gems.


